Subject: ef.f: stop using the non-standard FLUSH(unit) extension

WHAT IT FIXES
  ef.f both declares a COMMON block called FLUSH and calls a subroutine
  called FLUSH, so f2c refuses the file outright:

      Error on line 153 of ef.f: flush cannot be a subprogram:
                                 it is a common block.

  (f2c still exits 0 and still writes an ef.c, which is why the build
  script greps its output for "Error on line" rather than trusting the
  exit status.)

  Both halves are also wrong for wasm on their own:

  1. `call flush(6)` / `call flush(11)`. FLUSH(unit) is a Unix f77
     extension, not Fortran 77, and libf2c's flush_() takes no argument.
     wasm-ld does not merge a call whose signature differs from the
     definition -- it links a TRAPPING STUB, and the module then dies at
     run time with a bare `RuntimeError: unreachable` and no message.
     Native linkers silently accept the mismatch.

  2. `COMMON/FLUSH/NFLUSH` makes f2c emit a data symbol named `flush_`,
     which collides with libf2c's flush_() function.

  The block is renamed FLUSHX and the calls MYFLSH; patches/shim.c provides
  `myflsh_`. NFLUSH is never assigned anywhere in MOPAC 7 (it appears only
  in this file), so it is always 0 from the zero-initialised COMMON and the
  calls are in fact unreachable -- but they still have to translate and link.

--- a/ef.f
+++ b/ef.f
@@ -50,7 +50,7 @@
      $U(MAXPAR,MAXPAR),DD,rmin,rmax,omin,xlamd,xlamd0,skal,
      $MODE,NSTEP,NEGREQ,IPRNT
       COMMON/THREADS/NUM_THREADS
-      COMMON/FLUSH/NFLUSH
+      COMMON/FLUSHX/NFLUSH
 
       DIMENSION IPOW(9), EIGVAL(MAXPAR),TVEC(MAXPAR),SVEC(MAXPAR),
      1FX(MAXPAR),HESSC(MAXHES),UC(MAXPAR**2),oldfx(maxpar),
@@ -150,8 +150,8 @@
      1' GRAD.:',F10.3,' HEAT:',G13.7)
             IF ( NFLUSH.NE.0 ) THEN
                IF ( MOD(NSTEP+1,NFLUSH).EQ.0) THEN
-                  call flush(6)
-                  call flush(11)
+                  call myflsh(6)
+                  call myflsh(11)
                ENDIF
             ENDIF
          ELSE
@@ -163,8 +163,8 @@
      1' GRAD.:',F10.3,' HEAT:',G13.7)
             IF ( NFLUSH.NE.0 ) THEN
                IF ( MOD(NSTEP+1,NFLUSH).EQ.0) THEN
-                  call flush(6)
-                  call flush(11)
+                  call myflsh(6)
+                  call myflsh(11)
                ENDIF
             ENDIF
          ENDIF
